Description: WYSIWYG editor and browser for structured web pages
 Amaya edits web pages as they look: text is typed, selected and restyled
 on the formatted page, while Amaya keeps a clean, valid document structure
 underneath (XHTML, HTML 4, CSS, MathML, SVG).  Structure, source, links and
 table-of-contents views are kept in step with the formatted view.  It also
 has a spell checker, printing, templates, and a simple web browser (http
 and https, forms, cookies; no JavaScript).
 .
 This is an unofficial port of Amaya 11.4.7, developed by W3C and Inria
 until 2012, to current Linux systems (wxWidgets 3.2, GTK 3, libcurl).
 .
 File > Preview in browser shows the page being edited in Firefox (or
 another browser, see the documentation); a helper script copies a site's
 login cookies from Firefox for File > Load cookies.
